<properties>
    <property id="autoLapEnabled" type="boolean">true</property>
    <!-- Grade-adjusted-speed multiplier (see
         ActivityController.updateGradeAndGap()). Originally a 5.0 guess,
         then raised to 20 (the settings.xml slider ceiling) after fitting
         HR(t+30s) ~ speed + grade against two real rides (skating-only
         seconds, |grade| outliers beyond 15% dropped as GPS/altitude
         noise) gave a coefficient around 33 to 44. That comment predicted
         the estimate should trend down as pumping technique kept
         improving; a third ride's same fit (skating-only, same outlier
         cutoff) came out around 9.5 to 10, confirming the downward trend,
         so lowered to 10.0. (An earlier check that mixed walking seconds
         into the fit got a negative coefficient; that was a confound:
         walking covers the uphill sections and skating the flat/downhill
         ones here, so raw grade tracks the walk/skate tag more than
         effort unless skating-only is enforced.) R^2 is still low (0.02
         to 0.10 across lags), so treat this as a rough per-ride estimate.
         Revisit once more rides are in and the per-ride estimates stop
         drifting. -->
    <property id="gradeAdjustCoefficient" type="float">10.0</property>
</properties>
